cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "AKANE Architecture experiments: checking a small LLM's answers from the outside"
abstract: >-
  Code, data, and results for small experiments in which a small language model
  (Gemma-2 2B) answers true/false and "X is a type of Y" questions and its
  answers are checked by parts placed outside it: the model's own consistency
  rules with belief propagation, retrieved evidence, dictionary definitions with
  an NLI model, and definition chains in which the model only picks word senses.
  Plans were fixed before results; ties and losses are reported.
authors:
